WEBVTT

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:51.860
What's that?

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:52.710
Lan Evo?!

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:54.720
Is there such a Lan Evo in the Shutokou Area?

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:58.710
Who's that guy?

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:09.870
<i>In the evening heat</i>

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.360
This is the previous muffler.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:20.150
And on the left is Shige's muffler
currently installed on the BlackBird.

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:22.450
It's certain the power has reduced.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:26.230
The line is generally uneven and nearing the peak...

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:31.750
The horsepower is lessened by 5-8% at normal speed level,

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:35.040
and around 70hp is lost at the peak.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.880
So it really just sounds good.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.550
But even at this level, why does if feel so good during actual driving?

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:44.780
It seems the secret lies with the torque characteristic.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.020
Please look at this curve.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:51.430
At the start it's easy and the torque value isn't that great too,

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:54.030
but it doesn't drop until nearing the peak level.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:56.190
This will make it feel good,

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:58.240
and the driver can step on the accelerator as much as he likes.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:03.530
Shige is really a magician, he has excellent sense.

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:11.050
Today is the 3rd day...

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:15.140
Isn't it fine? In return for the information
about BlackBird going to Osaka,

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:18.300
you promised to take me along until we meet BlackBird again.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:22.160
But appears today is the last day.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.020
What?

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:34.900
Well, it'll be nice seeing the changes in BlackBird's
driving style after replacing its muffle, right?

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:35.510
Yeah!

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:50.830
What's up with the way BlackBird's driving?

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:53.280
It's extremely rough. This is the first time I've seen it like this.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:05.530
<i>Muting the sound of this Z, the sound
of the BlackBird comes rushing to me.</i>

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:11.600
I know this sound.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:18.100
Well, how should I put it, the Z gives out a sound like this too.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:29.090
<i>The motivation towards driving, which I've lost
for some time is clearly coming back to me.</i>

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:40.220
A Lan Evo with a Naniwa number plate?

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:43.020
That reminds me, my customer also told me something like that.

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:48.850
The other day you told me that Kitami went to Osaka
to ask Shige to make a muffler for the BlackBird, right?

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:51.610
Yeah, what's this got to do with that?

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:56.880
Than Lan Evo with the Naniwa plate
also seems to produce a great sound.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:00.480
A nice smooth sound that you wouldn't
expect from a high-tone turbo car.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:06.840
<i>Maki, how are you?</i>

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:11.730
<i>You must be mad at me for leaving
without saying a word. Forgive me.</i>

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:15.420
<i>It's been a week since I arrived at Tokyo.</i>

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:19.770
<i>As soon as I arrived here, I rented a 6-mat room without a bathroom.</i>

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:22.290
<i>Even so, I was surprised as it's really expensive.</i>

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:26.520
<i>I've also decided to work at the family
restaurant near my apartment.</i>

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:31.770
<i>It's so much different from before, where I was called boss and all.</i>

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:34.370
<i>I was trained by a part-timer who's an undergraduate.</i>

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:39.140
<i>Since it's just a part-time job, I don't
earn much even if I work every day.</i>

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:43.830
<i>But it's enough, since I didn't come here for work.</i>

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:50.280
<i>When I'm not working, I'm always driving.</i>

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:59.540
<i>Unexpectedly, the rumored Shutokou is quite difficult.</i>

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:04.090
<i>There are so many joints and branches
and I can't remember them all.</i>

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:11.290
<i>There are some fairly fast drivers here and there,
but I've not yet met anyone who's really fast.</i>

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:16.440
<i>Maki and Eriko-san too...</i>

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:21.600
<i>I'll forget about you for this three months.</i>

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:28.190
<i>During these three months given to me, I'll be a Tokyo person.</i>

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:34.450
<i>I'll live only for my car, I'll get by.</i>

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:45.290
<i>Xenon headlights... he's fast!</i>

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.510
<i>It has an RGO sticker on the front of it...</i>

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:55.010
<i>It must be a car from a workshop... interesting.</i>

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:01.860
A nice sounding Lan Evo with a Naniwa license plate.

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:04.110
Seems like this is the guy.

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:05.400
Why don't you try him out?

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:07.400
In 5 minutes, you'll know if he's the real deal or not, right?

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:12.900
Yeah, it's also a good time to check out the
engine that you rebuilt for the first time.

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:22.870
Wow, he's fast!

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:30.790
This car is fast. It has a different aura.

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:33.470
It's the first real challenge I've come across after coming to Tokyo!

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:47.440
What crazy moves, this slalom is something else!

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:53.020
I see, this is the rumored Lan Evo.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:55.450
Good, he's keeping up nicely.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:08:03.680
Oh, now I remember! RGO is Ohta Kazuo's RGO Speed Factory.

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:06.210
One of the most successful tuners.

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:12.400
This sound that's chasing us...

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:16.230
Just as Yamamoto said, this is Shige's sound.

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:36.640
Hey, your car sounds pretty good. Is Shige doing well?

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:39.060
Huh, you know Shige-san?

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:40.950
Yes, I know him very well.

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:44.330
I'm Ohta. This is my daughter, Rikako.

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:47.880
Oh, Yama, you're still here?

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:50.910
Something is bugging me. How was it?

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:55.180
It's so-so. Oh, this is my mechanic, Yamanaka.

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:59.220
Nice to meet you, I'm Kamiya Eiji, from Osaka.

00:08:59.220 --> 00:08:59.850
Hi.

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:04.860
That's a fast looking Lan Evo.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:06.520
How fast is it?

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:09.200
I think it's around 400hp.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:10.610
Can I have a look at it?

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:13.610
Sure, I don't mind.

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:16.610
I see.

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:19.430
Even with a small turbine, it seems to be able to rev all the way up.

00:09:20.270 --> 00:09:21.770
You're right.

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:25.620
It looks like it's put together effectively without any loss, but...

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:32.680
If you have time, wanna go for a spin with me?

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:34.640
You sure? I'd love to!

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:38.120
Alright, let's talk about Shige while driving then.

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:40.700
Well then, Yama, it's about time to close the shop.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:41.650
Alright.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:53.270
The R was put together nicely, huh?

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:56.340
Really? But my dad didn't say anything about it...

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:58.150
That's because our boss is a shy person.

00:09:58.770 --> 00:10:01.300
It's the first time you assembled an RB26, right?

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:04.670
Yeah, he suddenly told me to build it.

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:08.160
Frankly, I was very impressed, you did very well for your first time.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.340
Is that flattery?

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:14.200
Not at all. I thought it was as expected of you.

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:20.200
Of course, you still don't have enough experience
and the parts aren't really well assembled.

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:23.190
But, there's something that cannot be
obtained even with experience.

00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:28.390
That is a sense of cars. Rikako-san,
you have the same sense as the boss.

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:32.400
You'll be bored being a normal university student soon.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:39.360
It's like this. At a glance, you can tell that the torque valley disappears, right?

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:43.120
This way we can revise the negative parts of Shige's muffler.

00:10:43.670 --> 00:10:46.500
And there's a more interesting bit of data that appeared.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:48.870
Did you realize that your driving style has changed?

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:54.580
It doesn't seem like you changed because of Shige's data.

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:58.120
The time duration of opening the throttle is quite long.

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:01.870
Putting it nicely, you're being aggressive, but in
other words, the way you accelerate is rough.

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:06.600
But the speed is faster than I expected.
And strangely, the combustion looks good.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:10.060
Right now, you don't seem to be interested on visible data.

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:14.020
Yes, I've always been driving my car using logic alone.

00:11:14.550 --> 00:11:18.240
But now, I want to drive my car according to what I feel.

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:23.240
You might lose your rationality because of it.

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:33.700
A first generation Z which is faster than an R?

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:37.590
I heard it's called something like the Devil Z.

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:40.430
Yes, there is a Z like that.

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:43.390
Did you came to Tokyo because you wanted to see that car?

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:46.100
No, not really.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.600
You'll meet it, it just depends on you.

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:53.730
If your desire to meet it is true, you'll see it soon.

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:55.110
That's the kind of car it is.

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:00.970
By the way, how's this car?

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:03.620
It's good, it seems to turn quickly.

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:08.180
It's pretty good considering it was her
first time assembling an RB26.

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:09.300
First time?!

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:12.320
My daughter. She assembled this engine.

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:25.060
BlackBird.

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:33.050
That guy comes here every day,
in order to collect data for Shige's muffler.

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:40.570
Listen, if you're like him, chasing after
the Z, the first thing you need is power.

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:42.060
Power?

00:12:42.060 --> 00:12:47.790
If you don't get your hands on amazing
power, you won't be a match for that Z.

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:06.910
Welcome home.

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:09.810
Wanna have some coffee inside?

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:11.860
Yeah.

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:14.480
Is this really the first RB you assembled?

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:19.480
That's right. My dad always said that as long as
you can assemble an L-type, then you'll be fine.

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:22.850
Since we specialize in dealing with modified cars,

00:13:22.850 --> 00:13:24.620
there were many unused engines, especially L-types,

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:27.310
lying around the warehouse.

00:13:27.310 --> 00:13:31.980
The first engine I dismantled was also an L-type,
during my 2nd grade of Junior High School.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:34.500
Of course, I couldn't reassemble it.

00:13:36.990 --> 00:13:41.250
Since it was interesting, I totally took
apart the engine in the warehouse.

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:44.720
"If you can't assemble it, then don't
dismantle it!", I was scolded very badly.

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:49.480
"But they're just scraps!", I said. "Idiot, we'll use them one day."

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:51.540
I'm sure that he never used them at all.

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:57.480
So, you're working at a family restaurant now?

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:01.370
Yes, I still need to make a living.

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:04.850
Why don't you work here with us?

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:11.740
You'll learn a lot. You understand engines and you can drive well.

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:14.400
I'm being serious.

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:17.460
Thank you very much, but...

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:19.930
You don't want to? Why?

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:22.470
The family restaurant job is just to make a living, right?

00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:28.510
Yes, but I came to Tokyo with a promise
of returning in three months.

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:29.960
Even if I work only halfway...

00:14:32.070 --> 00:14:33.980
Three months, huh...

00:14:33.980 --> 00:14:38.050
Instead, please let me help you during
my free time. You don't have to pay me.

00:14:38.050 --> 00:14:40.470
Odd jobs are good enough.

00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:42.890
I see... alright, I understand.

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:46.750
Do as you please. I'll consider your salary.

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:50.780
It's alright, I'll really work for free. Is it ok if I start tomorrow?

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:51.480
Sure.

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:54.090
Thank you very much.

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:12.630
Hello.

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:17.070
Oh, you came. This is my wife, Yoko.

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:20.010
Actually, she's the queen who controls RGO.

00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:22.140
Geez, what are you saying...

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:25.920
This is Kamiya Eiji, whom I spoke about this morning.

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:28.160
He'll be helping around from today onwards.

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:29.830
I see, nice to meet you.

00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:32.650
Yes, it's a pleasure meeting you too.

00:15:34.360 --> 00:15:38.070
Even if you try following the way we speak,
it doesn't suit you at all.

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:55.880
<i>A car is coming.</i>

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.140
<i>FD, huh...</i>

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:05.520
<i>Their skill is around that of the lower middle class.</i>

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:13.550
Oh, the Benz behind is picking a fight.

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:14.810
Go ahead!

00:16:14.810 --> 00:16:15.530
Alright!

00:16:35.540 --> 00:16:38.070
<i>I'm not at that age anymore, huh.</i>

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:45.200
Yama-san, where should I put this?

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.660
Carry them into the factory.

00:16:47.660 --> 00:16:48.570
I got it.

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:51.760
Let me help.

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:53.080
Thank you.

00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:00.770
This engine, did you assembled it alone?

00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:02.080
Yeah, that's right.

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:05.280
I want to ride on it once. Is it ok?

00:17:05.280 --> 00:17:06.070
Sure.

00:17:06.070 --> 00:17:07.340
Tonight then.

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:15.090
The engine is original, only the pistons
and camshafts are special parts.

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:18.830
After that, it's just a repeating process
of balancing and fine-tuning.

00:17:18.830 --> 00:17:20.810
Nothing fancy at all.

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:26.180
The turbine is manufactured using pure metal, the exhaust manifold is Shige-san's Special.

00:17:26.180 --> 00:17:30.310
Then, rev up to 8000rpm for a full
boost and just turn the car with guts.

00:17:30.310 --> 00:17:32.530
You really are plain, huh?

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:33.440
Leave me alone.

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:35.750
But it's pretty fast.

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:39.960
Furthermore without additional load and with
good shift work, the speed picks up really well.

00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:42.160
Why don't you just be honest and say that I'm skilled?

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:48.120
What happened?

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:51.160
Behind us, there's a car catching up.

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:52.880
At this speed?

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:56.390
It's catching up. It's fast!

00:17:58.210 --> 00:18:01.220
<i>You'll meet it, it just depends on you.</i>

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:04.470
<i>If your desire to meet it is true.</i>

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:05.890
<i>That's the kind of car it is.</i>

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:08.450
<i>A Naniwa number plate.</i>

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:13.930
<i>And this sound. It's the same sound as BlackBird's.</i>

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:24.970
<i>At the moment, this guy Akio is driving it.</i>

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:27.030
<i>He should be around your younger brother's age.</i>

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:34.720
L28 Custom Twin Turbo,

00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:38.940
an S30Z which outputs 600hp.

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:40.430
600hp with an L-Type?!

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:42.870
You might now believe it, but it's true.

00:18:43.690 --> 00:18:46.390
That's Kitami's tuned Devil Z.

00:18:57.980 --> 00:19:01.190
<i>If he pulls away too much, he waits. If I catch up, he pulls away.</i>

00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:06.620
<i>He's matching my speed, as if he's
teaching me the rules of this place.</i>

00:19:07.150 --> 00:19:10.630
L-Type Twin Turbo. 600hp.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.260
<i>His speed increased all at once!</i>

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:32.860
<i>I can't keep up with him any more.</i>

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:36.320
<i>Your car is not bad.</i>

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:40.480
<i>A driving style which suits yourself and
doesn't depend on power is also good.</i>

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:46.620
<i>But we have our own way of doing things in Shutokou.</i>

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:49.620
<i>That's more power and more torque.</i>

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:53.500
<i>All those troublesome theories are instantly blown away.</i>

00:19:55.510 --> 00:19:57.250
<i>More power and more torque.</i>

00:20:02.370 --> 00:20:04.760
The other day, I met Eiji-san.

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:08.130
He was sitting next to RGO's Ohta.

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:13.950
An acquaintance from Osaka, huh?
Does he use Shige's muffler too?

00:20:13.950 --> 00:20:16.480
He does, it has a good sound.

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:20.590
He should understand that it doesn't rev much at high speeds, right?

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:24.620
Tomorrow, bring your car over to my place.

00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:29.230
I will delete all the current ECU settings and reprogram it.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:33.830
I'll eliminate the negative parts of Shige's muffler completely.

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:37.890
It might end up being a boring car hat's just fast, but let's do it.

00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:41.580
If Shige's a pro, we are also pros.

00:20:43.600 --> 00:20:46.210
<i>Only a Porsche Turbo is a true turbo car.</i>

00:20:46.210 --> 00:20:49.500
<i>Local turbo cars are totally different.</i>

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:50.640
<i>See you next time.</i>

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:54.600
<i>Goodbye. Drive Go Go.</i>

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:59.010
What "Drive Go Go"...  I was really into it.

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:04.490
<i>I couldn't step on.</i>

00:21:05.850 --> 00:21:09.150
<i>I wonder when it started, that I couldn't accelerate any further.</i>

00:21:15.030 --> 00:21:17.750
You're trying to get a clean reading, huh?

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:21.300
Hey, can you let me ride your car one more time?

00:21:31.220 --> 00:21:33.150
Why don't you spill out what you're thinking now?

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:35.770
It's about the Z the other day, right?

00:21:37.590 --> 00:21:41.010
It was incredible. That 600hp L-Type Z.

00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:42.770
Yeah.

00:21:43.550 --> 00:21:46.470
Eiji-san, did you came to Tokyo with that as a target?

00:21:46.470 --> 00:21:49.130
No, not really.

00:21:49.130 --> 00:21:51.040
But you want to win it, right?

00:21:51.040 --> 00:21:52.750
Yes, I do.

00:21:53.440 --> 00:21:57.190
Eiji-san, your Lan evo is really good.

00:21:57.190 --> 00:22:00.230
But it's surely impossible to chase that Z.

00:22:00.230 --> 00:22:01.760
If I leave as it is.

00:22:01.760 --> 00:22:05.500
Yes, so will you let me assemble it?

00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:08.710
What kind of changes to the specs do you have in mind?

00:22:08.710 --> 00:22:10.470
First, increase the displacement volume.

00:22:11.420 --> 00:22:16.550
For a 2 liter Direct 4 engine, the line is slow,
so I'll upgrade the stroke to make it 2.2 liter.

00:22:16.550 --> 00:22:19.420
The peak power is at around 7000rpm.

00:22:19.420 --> 00:22:21.500
Maximum torque is at around 5000rpm.

00:22:22.840 --> 00:22:26.220
The turbine can be left just as it is or made one level bigger.

00:22:26.220 --> 00:22:29.730
The boost pressure up to  max of 1.2kg.

00:22:29.730 --> 00:22:34.410
And if possible, making it a 4 Throttle and changing the final gear.

00:22:34.960 --> 00:22:39.250
If it's a Germany import, at 5th gear
with 7000rpm you can hit 260km/h.

00:22:39.860 --> 00:22:43.960
If it's more than 7500rpm, it will definitely hit 300km/h.

00:22:44.480 --> 00:22:50.460
With that, you can conquer both the
BlackBird and that S30Z with 600hp.

00:22:51.570 --> 00:22:53.970
So how much is the increase in power?

00:22:54.560 --> 00:22:56.190
Plus 50hp.

00:22:56.190 --> 00:23:00.360
This Lan Evo, with 450hp, can beat both the BlackBird and Z.

00:23:04.120 --> 00:23:05.140
I got it.

00:23:07.430 --> 00:23:08.220
I've decided.

00:23:09.440 --> 00:23:12.070
I'll leave this Lan Evo all up to you.
